@startuml
' Same-file reactive sync between two panes, with double echo-suppression.
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #333333
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #D6E4F0
  ParticipantFontColor #10223A
}

participant "Pane A\n(origin)" as A #D6E4F0
participant "doc-stream\nSubject (ws,uri)" as S #F5E9D0
participant "Pane B\n(peer)" as B #D6E4F0

== User types in Pane A ==
A -> A : updateListener fires\n(user edit, not annotated)
A -> A : has-peers? → true
A -> S : publish-delta!\n{origin=A, changes, seq}
S -> A : delivers to A's subscriber
note right of A #FADBD8
  Guard 1: origin == own pane-id
  → Pane A IGNORES its own delta
end note
S -> B : delivers to B's subscriber
B -> B : origin (A) ≠ own pane-id → accept
B -> B : apply-remote-delta!\n(annotated external-set)
note right of B #D5F5E3
  Guard 2: applied with external-set
  annotation → B's updateListener treats
  it as API-driven → no re-publish,
  no "user edit" LSP path. Cursor rebases
  via selection.map.
end note

== Result ==
note over A, B: Both panes converged. One coalesced LSP didChange is produced per file.
@enduml
